  "mach:judgement": "Caution",
  "mach:judgementReason": "Established and well-funded real-time outbreak surveillance system (2006, Boston Children's Hospital) with broader and faster signal coverage than WHO DON. However, there is no public API and data access is governed by a proprietary user agreement with Children's Hospital Boston, not an open license — limiting programmatic integration. Caution for teams needing open, reusable data; the platform remains useful for manual monitoring and situational awareness. Re-assess if an open API or data licence is introduced.",
  "mach:editorialReviewedAt": "2026-05-21",
